.data:100A3F10 aASpecialNoteAb db 0Ah		       ; DATA XREF: sub_1005A150+27o
.data:100A3F10		       db '*** A special note about internal error number 1007 ***',0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db 0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db 'Experience suggests that a common cause of i.e. 1007',0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db 'is unreliable memory or other hardware.  The 1007 assertion',0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db 'just happens to cross-check the results of huge numbers of',0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db 'memory reads/writes, and so acts (unintendedly) as a stress',0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db 'test of your memory system.',0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db 0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db 'I suggest the following: try compressing the file again,',0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db 'possibly monitoring progress in detail with the -vv flag.',0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db 0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db '* If the error cannot be reproduced, and/or happens at different',0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db '  points in compression, you may have a flaky memory system.',0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db '  Try a memory-test program.  I have used Memtest86',0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db '  (www.memtest86.com).  At the time of writing it is free (GPLd).'
.data:100A3F10		       db 0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db '  Memtest86 tests memory much more thorougly than your BIOSs',0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db '  power-on test, and may find failures that the BIOS doesn',27h,'t.',0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db 0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db '* If the error can be repeatably reproduced, this is a bug in',0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db '  bzip2, and I would very much like to hear about it.  Please',0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db '  let me know, and, ideally, save a copy of the file causing the',0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db '  problem -- without which I will be unable to investigate it.',0Ah
.data:100A3F10		       db 0Ah,0
.data:100A4331		       align 4
.data:100A4334 aBzip2Libbzip2I db 0Ah		       ; DATA XREF: sub_1005A150+Co
.data:100A4334		       db 0Ah
.data:100A4334		       db 'bzip2/libbzip2: internal error number %d.',0Ah
.data:100A4334		       db 'This is a bug in bzip2/libbzip2, %s.',0Ah
.data:100A4334		       db 'Please report it to me at: jseward@bzip.org.  If this happened',0Ah
.data:100A4334		       db 'when you were using some program which uses libbzip2 as a',0Ah
.data:100A4334		       db 'component, you should also report this bug to the author(s)',0Ah
.data:100A4334		       db 'of that program.  Please make an effort to report this bug;',0Ah
.data:100A4334		       db 'timely and accurate bug reports eventually lead to higher',0Ah
.data:100A4334		       db 'quality software.  Thanks.  Julian Seward, 15 February 2005.',0Ah
.data:100A4334		       db 0Ah,0
.data:100A44EF		       align 10h
